{
    "background_story": "Kade was a young Dinka tribesman from the war-torn regions of South Sudan. Growing up amidst conflict and displacement, he learned to rely on his community and traditional ways for survival. Kade's family was known for their exceptional cattle-herding skills, a vital part of Dinka culture. As he came of age, Kade took great pride in learning the ancient techniques and stories passed down through generations. He became particularly skilled in playing the traditional Dinka flute, using its haunting melodies to communicate with his cattle and calm them during times of stress. When his village was threatened by rival factions, Kade used his knowledge of the land and his flute-playing to help guide his people to safety. His bravery and dedication to his community earned him great respect among his peers, and he became a leader in preserving Dinka traditions.",
